--- !u!114 &40409706
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 40409705}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ea768deea00c4ad4ea64024f2e793b0f, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueInteractable
  npcName: Supervisor Franklin
  npcPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 85622a530d3f9e044bece05b21119254, type: 3}
  playerName: Detective Frankcesca
  playerPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 85622a530d3f9e044bece05b21119254, type: 3}
  lines:
  - speaker: 1
    text: " I\u2019ve been notified that you had the investigation extended."
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 94b00f3b25745594995d21cd7ff031b5, type: 3}
  - speaker: 0
    text: "Yes, sir, I did. I understand I was supposed to close the case, but\u2026
      I think Frank was investigating something worth following. I couldn\u2019t,
      in good conscience, close the case."
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4050df47d37b2fd45adc78d43e2cdd48, type: 3}
  - speaker: 1
    text: ' I see. The Bureau knew he''d been looking outside his assigned cases.
      Frank wasn''t particularly discreet about it toward the end.

'
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bcf3405be2f4be74fbd8ab182b99b812, type: 3}
  - speaker: 0
    text: "Then why wasn't that in the preliminary report? Isn\u2019t that something
      that should\u2019ve been investigated or at least noted?\r\n"
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0b797c841960d0f4e908c3bf2ef70017, type: 3}
  - speaker: 1
    text: ' Because the fact that he was looking at those files wasn''t unexpected.
      He''d always been obsessive. You know that. If there was a discrepancy in a
      report, Frank would sit with it until he''d convinced himself he''d found the
      reason. That''s part of what made him good. But there came a point where the
      discrepancy itself became proof to him that something was wrong. Eventually,
      every perceived link between evidence became a conspiracy. He most likely made
      some groundless link between cases and chased it.

'
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9350e748c87023140937bb0a8630ce55, type: 3}
  - speaker: 0
    text: 'That''s not what Frank thought. There''s clearly something there..

'
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 54cc1f6f8c8e06a47aeb69acf6d68701, type: 3}
  - speaker: 1
    text: ' Listen, like I said, Frank was obsessive, and he wasn''t in a very good
      state to judge that by the end. He wasn''t in a healthy space mentally. Everyone
      in the office witnessed it.

'
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e1d59e4a5717e324690f4c812aa80853, type: 3}
  - speaker: 0
    text: " Maybe you\u2019re right that he was in some psychotic episode, but I
      just- I don\u2019t want to immediately come to the easy conclusion. I need
      to be thorough - it\u2019s my job.\r\n"
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0452c33634ead4d469bcc0b64887bfac, type: 3}
  - speaker: 0
    text: '  I know. Look, if you find something that contradicts the official record,
      bring it to me. That''s the protocol. We''ll speak about it if it comes down
      to that.



'
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: af68bd8c23c390640b2aa549b5a77c48, type: 3}
